{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  THE MENU — a bottom sheet with detents, pushed sub-views and most-used tiles
  REFERENCE §7.4 · design/MobileMenu.dc.html · skill §4, §10 · docs/handoff/MENU-SHEET.md
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  Destroyed and written again on 4 Oct 2026 for the owner's request ("The menu for mobile
  should be smarter. You cannot currently drag down to close." — GAPS §8e). What the Phase 2
  sheet did is inventoried in docs/handoff/inventory/partials--menu-sheet.md and every
  MUST RESTORE row lives here, in menu-sheet.css or in menu-sheet.js.

  ── DETENTS, NOT A FIXED TOP ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

  The sheet is laid out at its FULL height and `menu-sheet.js` moves it with a transform:
  it opens at the medium detent (50% of the screen, Apple's `.medium` and Material's
  half-expanded ratio), drags up to full, and drags or flicks down to close. Every gesture
  has a control beside it (WCAG 2.5.7): the grabber is a button that toggles the two
  heights, and close, Esc and Back close. Without script the sheet never opens at all — the
  Menu tab is a script control — so none of this has a no-script half to fall back to.

  ── ONE CATALOGUE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Every destination drawn here — tile, Explore row, Help row, Notifications — comes from
  `menu_shortcuts()` (Services\MenuShortcuts), which knows who may open each one. So a
  most-used tile is always a destination this visitor could have scrolled to, and a
  signed-in member is not offered "Register a profile", which would send them to /account.

  The four squares are the visitor's most used (`personal`) or the Participate four until
  there is enough history. A Participate default pushed out of the squares heads Explore,
  so nothing becomes unreachable for not having been used. A member's are ranked on the
  server; a guest's in the browser, from the `<template>` below and the numbers in
  `data-ag-menu-params` — only when Preferences allows keeping anything.

  ── WHAT IS THE PHASE FILE'S AND WHAT IS THE DC'S ───────────────────────────

  The Explore list is §7.4's — Discover, Pulse, Giving, Shop, Legacy Vault, Blog, Register.
  The DC draws Leaderboard where the phase file says Blog; the phase file outranks the DC
  (REFERENCE §0). Every size, gap and radius is the DC's. The points figure is DM Sans with
  tabular figures, not the DC's mono (owner, GAPS Q5); the wordmark line is `--ag-soft`, not
  the DC's `--ag-mute`, which is never a word.

  ── STATUS SAYS WHAT WAS MEASURED, OR NOTHING ───────────────────────────────

  `status_light()` is the last state the scheduled check RECORDED, and null when that record
  is stale or missing — and then the row carries no state at all.

  ── COOKIES IS THE CONSENT HOOK ─────────────────────────────────────────────

  `/cookies#choices` with `data-ag-do="consent-open"`: consent.js opens the preferences sheet
  in place over this one and hands focus back to the Menu tab.
#}
{% import _self as ui %}

{% macro tile(q) %}
  <a class="ag-menu__tile" href="{{ q.href }}" data-ag-dest="{{ q.key }}">
    <span class="ag-menu__tile-i ag-tone--{{ q.tone }}" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="21" height="21" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="{{ q.d }}"></path></svg></span>
    <span class="ag-menu__tile-l">{{ q.label|trans }}</span>
  </a>
{% endmacro %}

{% macro row(i, extra) %}
  <a class="ag-list__row" href="{{ i.href }}" data-ag-dest="{{ i.key }}">
    <span class="ag-icon-tile ag-tone--{{ i.tone }}" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="{{ i.d }}"></path></svg></span>
    <span class="ag-list__label">{{ i.label|trans }}</span>
    {{ extra|default('') }}
    <span class="ag-list__chev" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ag-ico-dir" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"></path></svg></span>
  </a>
{% endmacro %}

{% set _ini = member_name ? (member_name|split(' ')|filter(w => w != '')|map(w => w|first)|join|upper|slice(0, 2)) : 'AG' %}
{% set _status = status_light() %}
{% set _m = menu_shortcuts() %}
{% set _chev %}<span class="ag-list__chev" aria-hidden="true"><svg class="ag-ico-dir" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m9 6 6 6-6 6"></path></svg></span>{% endset %}

<div class="ag-scrim ag-menu-scrim" data-ag-menu-scrim></div>

<div class="ag-sheet ag-menu" id="ag-menu" data-ag-menu-sheet role="dialog" aria-modal="true"
     aria-labelledby="ag-menu-title" inert
     data-ag-menu-who="{{ is_member ? 'member' : 'guest' }}"
     data-ag-menu-params="{{ _m.params|json_encode }}"
     data-title-main="{{ 'Menu'|trans }}" data-title-display="{{ 'Display & reading'|trans }}"
     data-title-lang="{{ 'Language'|trans }}"
     data-label-expand="{{ 'Expand menu'|trans }}" data-label-collapse="{{ 'Collapse menu'|trans }}">

  {# The top of the sheet is the handle a mouse drags by; a finger may drag anywhere. #}
  <div class="ag-menu__top" data-ag-menu-handle>
    <span class="ag-sheet__grabber" aria-hidden="true"></span>
    <div class="ag-sheet__head ag-menu__head">
      {# `hidden` on the main view, and the title keeps its column by `grid-column`, not by a
         placeholder: a `visibility:hidden` button is still in the focus list the shell
         builds on open, and focusing it fails silently, leaving focus on the tab behind. #}
      <button type="button" class="ag-appbar__icon ag-menu__back" data-ag-menu-back aria-label="{{ 'Back to menu'|trans }}" hidden>
        <svg class="ag-ico-dir" width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m15 18-6-6 6-6"></path></svg>
      </button>
      <h2 class="ag-menu__title" id="ag-menu-title" data-ag-menu-title>{{ 'Menu'|trans }}</h2>
      <button type="button" class="ag-appbar__icon ag-menu__close" data-ag-menu-close aria-label="{{ 'Close menu'|trans }}">
        <span class="ag-menu__x"><svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"></path></svg></span>
      </button>
    </div>
    {# The grabber as a control: Material's drag handle takes expand/collapse actions, and
       WCAG 2.5.7 asks a single-pointer way to do what the drag does. Drawn over the
       grabber, 44px tall; after the head in the DOM so focus on open lands on Close. #}
    <button type="button" class="ag-menu__grab" data-ag-menu-grab aria-label="{{ 'Expand menu'|trans }}"></button>
  </div>

  <div class="ag-sheet__body ag-menu__body" data-ag-menu-body>

    {# ── MAIN ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <div class="ag-menu__view" data-ag-menu-view="main">

      {% if is_member %}
        <a class="ag-menu__me" href="/account">
          <span class="ag-menu__av" aria-hidden="true">{{ _ini }}</span>
          <span class="ag-menu__who">
            <b class="ag-menu__name">{{ member_name|default('Your account'|trans) }}</b>
            <span class="ag-menu__view-p">{{ 'View your profile'|trans }}</span>
          </span>
          {# Null when unknown: left out rather than printed as a confident nought. #}
          {% set _pts = member_points() %}
          {% if _pts is not null %}
            <span class="ag-menu__pts"><b class="ag-num">{{ _pts|number_format }}</b><span>{{ 'points'|trans }}</span></span>
          {% endif %}
        </a>
      {% else %}
        <div class="ag-menu__join">
          <b class="ag-menu__join-t">{{ 'Join Africa GATES'|trans }}</b>
          <span class="ag-menu__join-p">{{ 'Nominate, vote and keep your recognitions in one place.'|trans }}</span>
          <a class="ag-menu__join-b" href="/account/login">{{ 'Sign in or join'|trans }}</a>
        </div>
      {% endif %}

      <nav class="ag-menu__quick" data-ag-menu-tiles
           aria-label="{{ _m.personal ? 'Most used'|trans : 'Participate'|trans }}"
           data-label-personal="{{ 'Most used'|trans }}">
        {% for q in _m.tiles %}{{ ui.tile(q) }}{% endfor %}
      </nav>

      <section class="ag-menu__sec" aria-labelledby="ag-menu-h-explore">
        <h3 class="ag-menu__h" id="ag-menu-h-explore">{{ 'Explore'|trans }}</h3>
        <div class="ag-list ag-menu__list" data-ag-menu-explore>
          {% for i in _m.displaced %}{{ ui.row(i) }}{% endfor %}
          {% for i in _m.explore %}{{ ui.row(i) }}{% endfor %}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ag-menu__sec" aria-labelledby="ag-menu-h-settings">
        <h3 class="ag-menu__h" id="ag-menu-h-settings">{{ 'Settings'|trans }}</h3>
        <div class="ag-list ag-menu__list">
          <button type="button" class="ag-list__row" data-ag-menu-to="display">
            <span class="ag-icon-tile ag-tone--set" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M4 7V5h16v2M9 19h6M12 5v14"></path></svg></span>
            <span class="ag-list__label">{{ 'Display & reading'|trans }}</span>
            <span class="ag-list__value" data-ag-size-label
                  data-l0="{{ 'Standard'|trans }}" data-l1="{{ 'Large'|trans }}" data-l2="{{ 'Largest'|trans }}">{{ 'Standard'|trans }}</span>
            {{ _chev }}
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="ag-list__row" data-ag-menu-to="lang">
            <span class="ag-icon-tile ag-tone--set" aria-hidden="true"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 12h18M12 3c2.5 2.7 3.8 5.7 3.8 9s-1.3 6.3-3.8 9c-2.5-2.7-3.8-5.7-3.8-9S9.5 5.7 12 3Z"></path></svg></span>
            <span class="ag-list__label">{{ 'Language'|trans }}</span>
            <span class="ag-list__value" lang="{{ lang() }}">{{ lang_name() }}</span>
            {{ _chev }}
          </button>
          {% for i in _m.settings %}{{ ui.row(i) }}{% endfor %}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="ag-menu__sec" aria-labelledby="ag-menu-h-help">
        <h3 class="ag-menu__h" id="ag-menu-h-help">{{ 'Help'|trans }}</h3>
        <div class="ag-list ag-menu__list">
          {% for i in _m.help %}
            {# Never the colour alone: the word is the state, the dot repeats it. #}
            {% set _live %}{% if i.key == 'status' and _status %}<span class="ag-menu__live ag-menu__live--{{ _status.status }}"><span class="ag-menu__dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>{{ _status.label|trans }}</span>{% endif %}{% endset %}
            {{ ui.row(i, _live) }}
          {% endfor %}
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="ag-menu__foot">
        <nav class="ag-menu__legal" aria-label="{{ 'Legal'|trans }}">
          <a href="/privacy">{{ 'Privacy'|trans }}</a>
          <a href="/terms">{{ 'Terms'|trans }}</a>
          <a href="/cookies#choices" data-ag-do="consent-open">{{ 'Cookies'|trans }}</a>
        </nav>
        {% if is_member %}
          {# A POST with the token, not a link a prefetch could follow. #}
          <form method="post" action="/account/logout" class="ag-menu__out">
            <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">
            <button type="submit" class="ag-menu__signout">{{ 'Sign out'|trans }}</button>
          </form>
        {% endif %}
        <span class="ag-menu__mark">{{ 'Africa GATES · An Afrovanguard initiative'|trans }}</span>
      </div>

      {# A guest's tiles are ranked in the browser: every destination they may open, as a
         tile and as a row, for the script to clone. Inert by nature — a <template>'s
         content is not in the document — and absent for a member, whose tiles the server
         ranked. #}
      {% if _m.all %}
        <template data-ag-menu-tpl>
          {% for q in _m.all %}<div data-for="{{ q.key }}">{{ ui.tile(q) }}{{ ui.row(q) }}</div>{% endfor %}
        </template>
      {% endif %}
    </div>

    {# ── DISPLAY & READING ─────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    <div class="ag-menu__view" data-ag-menu-view="display" hidden>
      <div class="ag-menu__card">
        {% include 'partials/display-reading.twig' with { uid: 'menu' } %}
      </div>
    </div>

    {# ── LANGUAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
    {# Links, not radios: following one navigates and the middleware stores the choice, so
       this works with scripting off. The name is in its own language with `lang`, and
       English below for somebody choosing on another person's behalf. #}
    <div class="ag-menu__view" data-ag-menu-view="lang" hidden>
      <div class="ag-list ag-menu__list" role="group" aria-label="{{ 'Language'|trans }}">
        {% for l in languages() %}
          <a class="ag-list__row ag-menu__lang" href="{{ lang_url(l.code) }}" hreflang="{{ l.code }}"
             {% if l.code == lang() %}aria-current="true"{% endif %}>
            <span class="ag-list__b">
              <span class="ag-list__label" lang="{{ l.code }}" dir="{{ l.dir }}">{{ l.name }}</span>
              <span class="ag-menu__en">{{ l.english|trans }}</span>
            </span>
            {% if l.code == lang() %}
              <svg class="ag-menu__tick" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 10.5 8.5 15 16 5.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg>
            {% endif %}
          </a>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
